  "slug": "lsst-gravitational-waves-66df",
  "summary": "New emulators, differentiable bispectra and field-level Lyman-α models target the accuracy and speed demanded by LSST Year 1 and DESI DR2-era analyses.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is fast, accurate theory and forward modeling for upcoming survey analyses. A Hi-COLA-trained emulator provides the nonlinear matter power spectrum in Cubic Galileon gravity, validated for LSST Year 1 weak lensing and clustering. bihalofit-JAX delivers a differentiable nonlinear bispectrum and projected statistics, reported to run orders of magnitude faster. For the Lyman-α forest, a cubic-order EFT field-level forward model validated on CAMELS and Sherwood yields BAO shift predictions and simulation-based priors, while a 3D U-Net maps density and velocity to flux, reproducing P1D, bispectrum and trispectrum across TNG and FLAMINGO. A secondary thread exploits alternative probes. Fast radio bursts give a first Ωm–w inference from 125 localized events alone, and, with IllustrisTNG, constraints on Ω_b f_ion across large-scale structure. A physics-informed neural network reconstructs w and the growth index from DESI DR2 to test GR, and Padé cosmography is forecast for LISA, ET and DECIGO sirens. The QCD equation-of-state study is peripheral.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-24"
}
